sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch03-13> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch03-13--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch03-13--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch03-13: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.43" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.434"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.5"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Interaction archives and trait databases can test visible matching between structures and partners for a biased but real subset of organisms. The universal and 'hidden' wording survives a null result, so discriminating power is low. What existing data can resolve is a proxy: whether known interactions predict form better than environment and phylogeny alone, in guilds that have both traits and links." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Ask what fraction of measured structures are statistically predictable from the traits of competitors, predators, prey, or escape targets, against a phylogeny-and-environment null. A large excess of matched structures would support pervasive relatedness of form; a null match rate would challenge the universal reading only for relations that are visible in the data." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Relations that are 'often hidden' can be postulated whenever a test finds no match, which blocks refutation.", "'Every' organism and 'essential' relation have no natural numerical threshold.", "Trait matching often restates known natural history (bill and prey size) for a few well-studied guilds." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch03-13--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch03-13--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch03-13--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch03-13--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch03-13 by Grok 4.7: 0.38" ;
